==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|goh|de}} {{m|goh|hantalōn}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈhandl̩n/|/ˈhandəln/|lang=de}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb-weak|handelt|handelte|gehandelt}}

# to [[trade]], to [[deal]]
#* '''2010''', ''[[w:Der Spiegel|Der Spiegel]]'', issue [http://www.spiegel.de/spiegel/print/index-2010-46.html 46/2010], page 95:
#*: In Toronto '''werden''' mehr als 1400 Bergbaubetriebe '''gehandelt''', jede Woche kommen im Schnitt drei Unternehmen hinzu.
#*:: More than 1400 mining companies are traded in Toronto, three companies are added each week on average.
# to [[negotiate]], [[haggle]]
# to [[act]], to [[take action]]
# {{label|de|with [[von]]}} to be about
#: Das Buch '''handelt von''' Äpfeln. — The book is about apples.
# {{label|de|reflexive|with [[um]]}} to be, to happen to be
#: Bei den Früchten in diesem Korb '''handelt es sich um''' Äpfel. — The fruits in this basket are apples.

